                              "note_tweet_results": {
                                "result": {
                                  "text": "DEMO / A longer field note\n\nThe morning train was unusually quiet. Most screens were dark. Someone was reading a paperback with a folded receipt for a bookmark.\n\nIt reminded me that reading is not the same thing as keeping up. A timeline can be an endless corridor, or it can be a stack of small letters. The difference is whether you get to finish one before the next asks for your attention.\n\nFor this little reader, each post keeps its own place. Long thoughts continue on another measured page. Refresh brings in a new stack without taking the letter out of your hands.\n\nThere are no videos here, no reply threads, no numbers asking you to react. Just original words, a way forward, and a way back.\n\nEnd of the sample long post. Try swiping up to return to the previous page."
                                }
                              }
