                                  "legacy": {
                                    "full_text": "DEMO / A note from the canal path\n\nLeave something unfinished for a walk. Sometimes the next useful thought arrives after you stop pushing for it.\n\nThe canal was quiet this morning. A heron waited beside the bridge, perfectly still while everyone hurried past. I stayed for a minute, then put my notebook away.\n\nOn the way home, the sentence I had been trying to finish finally arrived. It was shorter than the version on my desk. Most of the work was deciding what to leave out.\n\nA small experiment for tomorrow: take the same walk, bring the same question, and leave the phone in a pocket. There is room for a thought to change shape before it becomes a plan.",
                                    "created_at": "2026-11-03T07:00:00Z"
                                  }
                                }
